    <item>
      <title>Disney Profit Beats With Marvel Films Powering Streaming</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-11-17/disney-profit-beats-with-marvel-films-powering-streaming-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">7e5fd828c342a0413aa2506f</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:53:29 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Walt Disney reported sales and earnings that exceeded analysts’ expectations, with a particularly strong result in its streaming TV unit. Operating income in business that include the Disney+ and Hulu streaming services doubled to $824 million in the fiscal fourth quarter, due to higher subscription and ad revenue. Viewership of Marvel superhero-related programming more than doubled as fans caught up on the company’s catalog of Spider-Man and Avengers films, tied in part to theatrical releases from both this year, Disney said in a statement Tuesday. Geetha Ranganathan, Bloomberg Intelligence US Media Analyst said Disney earnings mean show a strong outlook for 2027. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
